\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {23}{\ignorespaces The $M = 5$ HSGP time basis functions. Left: the orthonormal eigenfunctions $\psi _l(t)$ on which the curvature root $g_{pk}(t)$ is expanded. Right: the pure concave curve $-\Psi _{ll}(t)$ each basis generates alone, the shape a metric loading only basis $l$ would exhibit. Basis 1 is the lowest-frequency, broadest bend; higher bases carry sharper, more localized curvature.\relax }}{61}{figure.caption.68}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:hsgp_time_basis}{{23}{61}{The $M = 5$ HSGP time basis functions. Left: the orthonormal eigenfunctions $\psi _l(t)$ on which the curvature root $g_{pk}(t)$ is expanded. Right: the pure concave curve $-\Psi _{ll}(t)$ each basis generates alone, the shape a metric loading only basis $l$ would exhibit. Basis 1 is the lowest-frequency, broadest bend; higher bases carry sharper, more localized curvature.\relax }{figure.caption.68}{}}
