\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {30}{\ignorespaces Canonical weight profile for Nikola Joki\'c, in the format of Figure~\ref  {fig:player_profile_kobe}. The OBPM panel is nearly identical to Bryant's ($0.92$ vs.\ $0.91$ on component 1), but the GP\% panel shows the display's distinctive information: energy split across components 1 and 2 ($0.51/0.42$) with a coherent \emph  {negative} interference weight of $-0.37$, near the Cauchy--Schwarz bound of $-\genfrac  {}{}{}1{1}{2}$. The anti-aligned components cancel $45$--$87\%$ of the diagonal bending across ages 28--37: the model encodes his durable availability by loading two canonical shapes against each other rather than by shrinking their loadings.\relax }}{68}{figure.caption.75}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:player_profile_jokic}{{30}{68}{Canonical weight profile for Nikola Joki\'c, in the format of Figure~\ref {fig:player_profile_kobe}. The OBPM panel is nearly identical to Bryant's ($0.92$ vs.\ $0.91$ on component 1), but the GP\% panel shows the display's distinctive information: energy split across components 1 and 2 ($0.51/0.42$) with a coherent \emph {negative} interference weight of $-0.37$, near the Cauchy--Schwarz bound of $-\tfrac {1}{2}$. The anti-aligned components cancel $45$--$87\%$ of the diagonal bending across ages 28--37: the model encodes his durable availability by loading two canonical shapes against each other rather than by shrinking their loadings.\relax }{figure.caption.75}{}}
